{
 "_comment": "Default corpus catalog shipped with Veritate. Each entry's stem is the on-disk basename (foo -> foo_train.bin / foo_val.bin in trainers/corpus/). format='raw_bytes' = direct URL written as a uint8 byte stream (Veritate trains byte-level, so plaintext bytes ARE tokens). format='hf_dataset' = stream rows from a HuggingFace dataset, encode each text column as UTF-8, separate rows with two newlines. format='native' = the bins ship inside the repo at veritate_mri/data/corpus/; install copies them into trainers/corpus/ with no network, and sizes are read from the bundled files. format='zip_bundle' = train_url is one hosted zip holding <stem>_train.bin + <stem>_val.bin; install extracts both and deletes the zip; sha256 fields verify the extracted bins. coming_soon=true disables install until the corpus is published: replace the PLACEHOLDER train_url with the real COS link and drop the flag to release. max_bytes_train caps how much of streaming HF data is written before stopping. val_split_ratio carves off the tail of the downloaded train file as val.bin when no separate val source is supplied. recommended_min_params / _max_params drive the training-tab size-mismatch warning. Size ladder rationale: developer_documentation/corpus/library_ladder.md. The dashboard prompts the user for confirmation before installing any corpus larger than 10 GB; the backend additionally requires confirm_large=true in the install body for those. Dashboard grouping: family = 'carpathian' (Carpathian-published families: chat/agent/mcp/code/sft) or 'public' (external published datasets: fineweb_edu, wikitext103, etc.). topic groups within a family (chat, agent, mcp, code, knowledge, market, special_sft). Both are advisory; if omitted the dashboard falls back to per-stem defaults.",
